WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.394
Every five years a large fair was held in Nottingham during the fall.

2
00:00:07.395 --> 00:00:11.326
The main event was always the archery contest.

3
00:00:11.327 --> 00:00:15.899
People came from far and wide to enjoy the events at the fair.

4
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.310
This year the sheriff hesitated to announce the fair.

5
00:00:19.311 --> 00:00:23.941
He didn't want Robin Hood and his men to make a fool of him again.

6
00:00:23.942 --> 00:00:27.978
"But if I don't hold the fair, people will laugh at me.

7
00:00:27.979 --> 00:00:31.175
They'll say I'm afraid of Robin Hood," he said.

8
00:00:31.176 --> 00:00:33.793
At last he had an idea.

9
00:00:33.794 --> 00:00:38.064
"What if I offer a prize that Robin Hood doesn't want?

10
00:00:38.065 --> 00:00:40.894
Then he won't come!"

11
00:00:40.895 --> 00:00:43.982
The sheriff announced the fair.

12
00:00:43.983 --> 00:00:50.483
This year the archery prize was two cows.

13
00:00:50.484 --> 00:00:54.409
When he heard the news, Robin was annoyed.

14
00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:58.825
"Usually the prize is gold," he complained to Little John.

15
00:00:58.826 --> 00:01:00.592
"I don't need cows!

16
00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:03.876
We have enough deer to eat here in the forest.

17
00:01:03.877 --> 00:01:06.550
It's not worth going to the fair."

18
00:01:06.551 --> 00:01:10.994
But Little John had heard some gossip at the Blue Boar Inn.

19
00:01:10.995 --> 00:01:16.611
"People are saying that the sheriff offered that prize so you wouldn't go to the fair.

20
00:01:16.612 --> 00:01:20.496
But I still want to win the archery contest!"

21
00:01:20.497 --> 00:01:22.717
Robin hesitated.

22
00:01:22.718 --> 00:01:29.027
Little John was his right-hand man, and he didn't want anything to happen to Little John.

23
00:01:29.028 --> 00:01:35.740
"You must wear a disguise, so the sheriff won't recognize you. And be careful!"

24
00:01:35.741 --> 00:01:40.301
Little John nodded. "I'll wear red instead of green.

25
00:01:40.302 --> 00:01:43.492
I'll pull up my hood to hide my face.

26
00:01:43.493 --> 00:01:52.281
And I'll call myself Reynold Greenleaf."

27
00:01:52.282 --> 00:01:58.292
Dressed in red, Little John took his bow and arrows to the Nottingham Fair.

28
00:01:58.293 --> 00:02:03.378
The fairgrounds looked festive, with booths selling food and drinks.

29
00:02:03.379 --> 00:02:13.398
Flower garlands hung from colorful tents, and people danced and sang.

30
00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:19.124
Women and men turned to look at Little John as he strolled through the fairgrounds.

31
00:02:19.125 --> 00:02:26.024
He was taller than all the other men there, with strong and broad shoulders.

32
00:02:26.025 --> 00:02:33.683
A big crowd gathered around a ring where men fought with staffs.

33
00:02:33.684 --> 00:02:38.120
The champion was Eric of Lincoln.

34
00:02:38.121 --> 00:02:42.179
Eric walked up and down, swinging his staff.

35
00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:47.250
"Is there a man from Nottingham brave enough to challenge me?"

36
00:02:47.251 --> 00:02:53.815
Men tried to coax other men to step into the ring, but everyone was afraid of Eric.

37
00:02:53.816 --> 00:02:57.910
Then Eric spotted Little John in the crowd.

38
00:02:57.911 --> 00:03:02.237
"Hey, you! Big fellow in red!" he called.

39
00:03:02.238 --> 00:03:07.178
"You look very strong! Surely, you will fight me."

40
00:03:07.179 --> 00:03:09.989
Little John couldn't resist.

41
00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:13.309
He borrowed a staff and entered the ring.

42
00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:16.369
Eric grinned and gazed at the crowd.

43
00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:19.202
"Watch, good people!" he boasted.

44
00:03:19.203 --> 00:03:23.346
"I'll defeat this fighter quickly."

45
00:03:23.347 --> 00:03:28.965
Eric attacked. Once, twice, three times, he struck at Little John.

46
00:03:28.966 --> 00:03:31.397
But he could not hit the man in red.

47
00:03:31.398 --> 00:03:36.138
The first fight ended, and the men stepped back.

48
00:03:36.139 --> 00:03:39.985
"This isn't going to be easy," said Eric to himself.

49
00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:43.877
The men circled each other again.

50
00:03:43.878 --> 00:03:45.896
Suddenly Eric attacked.

51
00:03:45.897 --> 00:03:51.245
But Little John met every blow with his own staff.

52
00:03:51.246 --> 00:03:54.037
Then Little John saw his chance.

53
00:03:54.038 --> 00:04:01.412
With a swinging blow, he knocked Eric to the ground.

54
00:04:01.413 --> 00:04:03.996
The crowd roared.

55
00:04:03.997 --> 00:04:08.532
People from other parts of the fair came running to see what was going on.

56
00:04:08.533 --> 00:04:15.075
Everyone applauded as Little John stepped out of the ring and returned his borrowed staff.

57
00:04:15.076 --> 00:04:18.413
Next it was time for the archery contest.

58
00:04:18.414 --> 00:04:21.894
The sheriff sat on a raised platform.

59
00:04:21.895 --> 00:04:26.498
He watched the archers as they arrived, looking for Robin Hood.

60
00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:31.529
"That thief didn't dare to come!" he said triumphantly.

61
00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:38.234
Twenty archers entered the contest and each took three shots.

62
00:04:38.235 --> 00:04:42.797
Of course, Little John was the best archer of all.

63
00:04:42.798 --> 00:04:46.350
The sheriff stepped down to award the prize.

64
00:04:46.351 --> 00:04:49.637
He stared closely at Little John.

65
00:04:49.638 --> 00:04:53.154
"I think I've seen you somewhere before."

66
00:04:53.155 --> 00:04:56.516
"That's probably true," said Little John.

67
00:04:56.517 --> 00:05:00.174
"I've often been in the crowd when you passed by."

68
00:05:00.175 --> 00:05:04.568
He boldly looked the sheriff in the eye.

69
00:05:04.569 --> 00:05:08.445
"I hear that you defeated Eric of Lincoln," said the sheriff.

70
00:05:08.446 --> 00:05:13.295
"You've made all of Nottingham proud. What's your name?"

71
00:05:13.296 --> 00:05:15.926
"Reynold Greenleaf."

72
00:05:15.927 --> 00:05:20.386
"Well, Reynold Greenleaf, how would you like to join my household?

73
00:05:20.387 --> 00:05:23.880
As my servant, you'll be clothed and well fed.

74
00:05:23.881 --> 00:05:29.261
I'll also give you a cash bonus every year. What do you say?"

75
00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:31.961
Little John chuckled to himself.

76
00:05:31.962 --> 00:05:36.336
It would be a great joke to live with the sheriff.

77
00:05:36.337 --> 00:05:40.157
"I'll gladly join you!" said Little John.

78
00:05:40.158 --> 00:05:44.123
"And I'll donate my prize to the people here."

79
00:05:44.124 --> 00:05:48.732
People cheered once more for Little John.

80
00:05:48.733 --> 00:05:53.268
Musicians began playing bagpipes and harps.

81
00:05:53.269 --> 00:05:59.752
As Little John followed the sheriff home, two cows roasted on the town green.

82
00:05:59.753 --> 00:06:04.418
Little John had to hide his smile.

83
00:06:04.419 --> 00:06:13.652
The sheriff had no idea that his new servant was Robin Hood's right-hand man!

